\subsection{Multi-Threshold Classification Performance}

Table~\ref{tab:sensitivity_b1} reports Task~B1 classification metrics across six NVE thresholds. Task~B1 achieves $\text{AUROC} = 0.917$ because exp\_059 (NVE${=}4.72\times$, self-correcting CIVO, B1-negative) ranks above two sustained-CIVO positives ($4.12\times$, $4.02\times$), breaking the perfect rank separation that held before its inclusion. The optimal threshold lies in the interval $(3.78, 4.02]$; we report $\geq 3.9\times$ as a representative value (accuracy $10/11 = 90.9\%$). Table~\ref{tab:sensitivity_b2} provides the corresponding analysis for Task~B2 ($\text{AUROC} = 0.967$, imperfect separation due to 008e\_v3\_s2).

